"archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/deployments","created_at":"2014-09-18T16:12:01Z","updated_at":"2026-03-11T08:09:26Z","pushed_at":"2026-03-10T23:39:43Z","git_url":"git://github.com/angular/angular.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:angular/angular.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/angular/angular.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/angular/angular","homepage":"https://angular.dev","size":616697,"stargazers_count":100153,"watchers_count":100153,"language":"TypeScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":27109,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1141,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["angular","javascript","pwa","typescript","web","web-framework","web-performance"],"visibility":"public","forks":27109,"open_issues":1141,"watchers":100153,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"**I'm submitting a ...**\n\n```\n[x] bug report => search github for a similar issue or PR before submitting\n[ ] feature request\n[ ] support request => Please do not submit support request here, instead see https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#question\n```\n\n**Current behavior**\nAs of rc.5, https calls that set Content-Type to 'application/json' fail this message:\n\n```\nTypeError: Cannot read property 'toString' of null\n    at Request.Body.text (https://localServer/path/main.bundle.js:176324:26)\n    at Request.getBody (https://localServer/path/prep/main.bundle.js:176883:29)\n    at Observable._subscribe (https://localServer/path/main.bundle.js:176187:37)\n    at Observable.subscribe (https://localServer/path/main.bundle.js:139:62)\n```\n\nThe error occurs in the last line of this function because this._body is null: \n\n``` typescript\n    Body.prototype.text = function () {\n        if (this._body instanceof url_search_params_1.URLSearchParams) {\n            return this._body.toString();\n        }\n        if (this._body instanceof ArrayBuffer) {\n            return String.fromCharCode.apply(null, new Uint16Array(this._body));\n        }\n        if (http_utils_1.isJsObject(this._body)) {\n            return lang_1.Json.stringify(this._body);\n        }\n        return this._body.toString();\n    };\n```\n\nThe change made for #9452 introduced this behavior by changing 'Content-Type' to 'content-type' in the header. Although the header values are supposed to be case-insensitive, this seems not to be the case in practice in this application.\n\nThe calls fail early enough that nothing appears in the Chrome Network tab.\n\nI can work around this by changing `normalize` in node_modules/@angular/http/src/headers.js to just return the argument, but that is not a sustainable solution.\n\n**Expected/desired behavior**\nHttps calls with headers succeed.\n\n**Reproduction of the problem**\nI don't know how to reproduce the problem with a plunker because a prerequisite is being able to make an https call, and I don't know how to do that in plunker.\n\nI'm able to reproduce it locally by having the following in my AppComponent (replacing the url as needed):\n\n``` typescript\n  constructor(http: Http) {\n    const config:RequestOptionsArgs = {headers: new Headers()};\n    config.headers.append('Content-Type', 'application/json');\n\n    http.get('https://localServer/path/', config).toPromise()\n      .then(response => console.log('response', response));\n  }\n```\n\n**What is the expected behavior?**\nHttps calls with headers succeed.\n\n**What is the motivation / use case for changing the behavior?**\nBeing able to define content-type as json on https calls.\n\n**Please tell us about your environment:**\n- **Angular version:** 2.0.0-rc.5\n- **Browser:** Chrome 52.0.2743.116 m and Firefox 35.01 \n- **Language:** TypeScript 2.0 \n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/10885/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/10885/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":790491528,"node_id":"MDE1OlJlZmVyZW5jZWRFdmVudDc5MDQ5MTUyOA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/events/790491528","actor":{"login":"hbkrunal","id":8793216,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3OTMyMTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8793216?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hbkrunal","html_url":"https://github.com/hbkrunal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hbkrunal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hbkrunal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hbkrunal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hbkrunal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hbkrunal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.g